Audit complete: **FAIL / NOT_LEGIT**.

The K proof reconstructs successfully and is non-vacuous, but proves an ASCII-only computation. For `"É"`, the trusted canonical returns `201` while the candidate and formal postcondition return `0`, materially violating the unrestricted string contract.

